hadiths[66]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16704","He said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Humayd al-Araj, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Muadh, from a man from the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed the people at Mina and settled them in their lodgings and said: Let the Muhajirun alight here, and he pointed to the right of the qibla, and the Ansar here, and he pointed to the left of the qibla, then let the people alight around them; he said: And he taught them their rites, and the ears of the people of Mina were opened until they heard him in their lodgings; he said: And I heard him say: Stone the jamra with the like of the pebbles of khadhf."
"16705","Abd Allah said: I heard Musab al-Zubayri say: Abu Talha al-Qass came to Malik ibn Anas and said: O Abu Abd Allah, people have forbidden me to narrate this hadith: May Allah bless Ibrahim, indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious, and upon Muhammad and upon his household and upon his wives; Malik said: Narrate it and tell it, and its wording."
"16707","He said: Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, he said: al-Ashjai narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-Amash, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from a man, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: There will be people having a covenant, and whoever kills a man among them will not smell the fragrance of Paradise, though its scent is indeed found from a journey of seventy years."
"16709","He said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed me, from Ata ibn al-Saib, he said: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hadrami say: one who heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say informed me: Indeed among my umma are people given the like of the rewards of its first, they denounce evil."
"16710","He said: Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Haritha ibn Mudarrib, from some of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his companions: Among you are men to whom I do not give anything, entrusting them; among them is Furat ibn Hayyan, he said: from Banu Ijl."
"16713","Muammal ibn Ismail Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to us, from Munib, from his uncle, he said: It reached a man, from a man from the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Whoever conceals his Muslim brother in this world, Allah will conceal him on the Day of Resurrection; so he journeyed to him while he was in Egypt and asked him about the hadith; he said: Yes, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever conceals his Muslim brother in this world, Allah will conceal him on the Day of Resurrection; he said: And I had heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"16716","He said: Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Shuba narrated to us, from Said al-Jurayri, he said: I heard Ubayd ibn al-Qaqa narrate to a man from Banu Hanzala, he said: A man watched the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying, and he began to say in his prayer: O Allah, forgive me my sin and widen for me my house and bless for me in what You provided me."
"16717","He said: Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Shuba narrated to us, from Abu Imran, he said: I said to Jundub: I have pledged these, meaning Ibn al-Zubayr, and they want me to go out with them to Sham; he said: Hold back; I said: They refuse; he said: Ransom yourself with your wealth; he said: I said: They refuse unless I strike with them with the sword; Jundub said: So-and-so narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The slain man will come with his killer on the Day of Resurrection and say: O Lord, ask this one for what he killed me; Shuba said: And I think he said: And he will say: For what did you kill him; and he will say: I killed him for the kingdom of so-and-so; he said: So Jundub said: So beware of it."
"16718","He said: Abu Nuh narrated to us, he said: Malik informed us, from Sumayy, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from a man from the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pour water on his head at al-Suqya, either from heat or from thirst, while he was fasting; then he remained fasting until he came to Kadid, then he called for water and broke his fast, and the people broke their fast, and it was the year of the conquest."
"16719","He said: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Anas informed us, from Sumayy, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith, from a man from the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fasted on a journey in the year of the conquest and ordered his companions to break their fast and said: You will meet an enemy of yours, so gain strength; it was said: O Messenger of Allah, the people have fasted due to your fasting; when he came to al-Kadid he broke his fast; he said: The one who narrated to me said: I indeed saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pouring water on his head from heat while he was fasting."
"16729","Rawh and Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, they said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Hasan ibn Muslim informed me, from Tawus, from a man who reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Circumambulation is only prayer, so when you circumambulate, speak little; and Ibn Bakr did not raise it."
"16731","He said: Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from al-Azraq ibn Qays, from Yahya ibn Yamar, from a man from the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first of what the servant is reckoned for is his prayer; if he completed it, it is written for him complete, and if he did not complete it, Allah, mighty and majestic, says: Look, do you find for My servant any voluntary act to complete thereby his obligation; then zakat likewise, then deeds are taken according to that."
"16732","He said: Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Muhallab ibn Abi Sufra, from a man from the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I do not see them tonight but they will attack you by night; if they do, your slogan is Ha Mim, they will not be aided."
"16733","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Tamima, from a man of his people, that he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or he said: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and a man came to him and said: Are you the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or he said: Are you Muhammad; he said: Yes; he said: To what do you call; he said: I call to Allah, mighty and majestic, alone, who when harm befalls you and you call upon Him, He removes it from you, and who when a year of drought strikes you and you call upon Him, He grows for you, and who when you are in a barren land and lose your way and call upon Him, He returns you; he said: So the man submitted, then said: Counsel me, O Messenger of Allah; he said to him: Do not revile anything, or he said: anyone, al-Hakam doubted; he said: So I have not reviled a camel nor a sheep since the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) counseled me; and do not disdain kindness, even with your face open toward your brother while you speak to him; and pour from your bucket into the vessel of one seeking water; and wear the izar to half the shin, and if you refuse, then to the ankles; and beware of trailing the izar, for it is from conceit, and Allah, blessed and exalted, does not love conceit."
"16734","He said: al-Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Muhajir al-Saigh, from an unnamed man from the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he heard a man, meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), recite: Say: O disbelievers; he said: As for this one, he is quit of shirk; and he heard another recite: Say: He is Allah, One; and said: As for this one, he has been forgiven."
"16735","He said: Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from some of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cauterized Sad or Asad ibn Zurara in the throat for the inflammation, and said: I will not leave in myself any distress for Sad or Asad ibn Zurara."
"16738","Abu Amir narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Yazid, meaning Ibn Jabir, from Khalid ibn al-Lajlaj, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Aish, from some of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to them one morning cheerful, bright of face or radiant of face; we said: O Messenger of Allah, we see you cheerful, bright of face or radiant of face; he said: And what prevents me, when my Lord, mighty and majestic, came to me tonight in the finest form and said: O Muhammad; I said: At Your service, my Lord, at Your aid; He said: In what does the highest assembly dispute; I said: I do not know, my Lord; He said that two or three times; he said: So He placed His two palms between my shoulders, and I felt its coolness between my breasts, until what is in the heavens and what is in the earth became manifest to me; then he recited this verse: And thus We show Ibrahim the kingdom of the heavens and the earth, that he may be of the certain; then He said: O Muhammad, in what does the highest assembly dispute; he said: I said: In expiations; He said: And what are expiations; I said: Walking on feet to the congregations, and sitting in the mosque after the prayers, and completing wudu in hardship; He said: Whoever does that lives well and dies well and is of his sin as on the day his mother bore him; and of degrees are good speech and giving salam and feeding food and prayer at night while people sleep; He said: O Muhammad, when you pray say: O Allah, I ask You good deeds and leaving evils and love of the poor, and that You turn to me, and when You intend a trial among people, take me to You untempted."
"16739","He said: al-Zubayri Muhammad ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Israil narrated to us, from Simak, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd Allah ibn Amir narrated to me, he said: one who heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he ordered the stoning of a man between Makkah and Madinah narrated to me; when he felt the touch of the stones he went out and fled; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why did you not leave him."
"16740","He said: Surayj ibn al-Numan narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq, from a man, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, when were you made a prophet; he said: While Adam was between spirit and body."
"17096","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Hariz narrated to us, he said: Shurahbil ibn Shuf'ah narrated to us, from one of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: It will be said to the children on the Day of Resurrection: Enter Paradise. He said: So they will say: O Lord, until our fathers and our mothers enter. He said: So they will come. He said: So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will say: Why do I see them withholding? Enter Paradise. He said: So they will say: O Lord, our fathers and our mothers. He said: So He will say: Enter Paradise, you and your fathers."
"17350","Haddathana Yaqub, he said haddathana my father, from Salih ibn Kaysan, Ibn Shihab said: Akhbarani Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah ibn Kab ibn Malik, that some of those who witnessed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Khaybar informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a man among those with him: This one is from the people of the Fire. When fighting came, the man fought most fiercely until wounds increased upon him, so men from the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, have you seen the man whom you mentioned is from the people of the Fire, for by Allah he has fought in the path of Allah most fiercely and wounds increased upon him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yet he is from the people of the Fire. And some people nearly doubted. While they were upon that, the man felt the pain of wounds, so the man reached with his hand to his quiver and pulled an arrow from it and killed himself with it. So a man from the Muslims hastened to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Prophet of Allah, Allah has confirmed your words, so-and-so has killed himself and killed his soul."
"17674","'Abd al-Samad narrated to us: 'Umar ibn Hamzah narrated to us: 'Ikrimah ibn Khalid narrated to us, who said: And a man from Banu Tamim spoke ill of him in his presence, so he took a handful of pebbles to pelt him with. Then 'Ikrimah said: So-and-so from among the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to me that Tamim were mentioned before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). A man said: This clan of Tamim has been slow concerning this matter. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked toward Muzaynah and said: No slower than them are these people. And a man said one day: These people of Tamim have been slow with their charities. He said: Red and black camels of Banu Tamim came forward, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: These are the camels of my people. And a man from Banu Tamim spoke ill in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day, and he said: Say nothing about Banu Tamim but good, for they are the longest of people in spears against the Dajjal."
"18214","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Awwam informed us, Abd al-Jabbar al-Khawlani narrated to us, he said: A man from the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque and there was Kab telling stories, so he said: Who is this. They said: Kab telling stories. So he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: None tells stories except a ruler or one appointed or one conceited. He said: That reached Kab, and he was never seen telling stories afterward."
"18215","Rawh narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar narrated to us from Ibn Shihab that Ata ibn Yazid narrated to him that one of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to him that he said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O Messenger of Allah, which people are best. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A believer striving with himself and his wealth in the cause of Allah Almighty. They said: Then who, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Then a believer in a mountain pass fearing Allah and sparing people his evil."
"18220","Ibrahim ibn Ishaq al-Talaqani narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us from Yahya ibn Hassan from a man of Banu Kinanah, he said: I prayed behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the year of the conquest and heard him say: O Allah, do not disgrace me on the Day of Resurrection. Ibn al-Mubarak said: Yahya ibn Hassan is from the people of Bayt al-Maqdis, and he was an old man of good understanding."
"18238","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Khalid al-Hadhdha from Abu Qilabah from Muhammad ibn Abi Aishah from a man from the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perhaps you recite while the imam recites, two or three times. They said: O Messenger of Allah, we do. He said: So do not do so except that one of you recites the Opening of the Book."
"18240","Waki narrated to us, my father narrated to us from Mansur from Hilal ibn Yasaf from al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah from a man from the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever kills a man of the protected people will not find the scent of Paradise, though its scent is found from seventy years travel."
"18241","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us from Shubah, and Muhammad ibn Jafar said: Shubah narrated to us from Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, he said: I heard Ibn Muhayriz narrating from a man from the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Some people of my community will drink wine calling it by another name."
"18242","Hushaym narrated to us, Dawud ibn Amr informed us, he said: Abu Sallam narrated to us, he said: One who saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to me that he urinated then recited something of the Quran, and Hushaym once said a verse of the Quran, before touching water."
"18471","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Hakim ibn Abi Yazid, from his father, from one who heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Leave the people, let some of them benefit from some, and when a man seeks counsel from his brother, let him advise him sincerely."
"18472","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Ata ibn al-Saib narrated to us, he said: The first day I knew Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, I saw an old man white in head and beard upon a donkey following a funeral, and I heard him say: So-and-so son of so-and-so narrated to me that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever loves meeting Allah, Allah loves meeting him, and whoever hates meeting Allah, Allah hates meeting him, and the people fell down weeping, so he said: What makes you weep, and they said: We hate death, he said: It is not that, but when death comes, if he is of those brought near, then rest and basil and a Garden of Bliss, and when given those tidings he loves meeting Allah, and Allah loves meeting him more, but if he is of the deniers astray, then a lodging of boiling water, Ata said: And in the reading of Ibn Masud: Then roasting in Hell, and when given those tidings he hates meeting Allah, and Allah hates meeting him more."
"18478","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abi al-Bakhtari al-Tai who said: One who heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed me that he said: People will not perish until they exhaust their excuses against themselves."
"18482","Ismail narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abi Burdah, from a man of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O people, repent to Allah and seek His forgiveness, for I repent to Allah and seek His forgiveness every day a hundred times, so I said to him: O Allah, I seek Your forgiveness, O Allah, I turn to You, is it two or one, and he said: That is it, or like this."
"19041","Haddathana Abd al-Razzaq, akhbarana Sufyan from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abis from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from a man from among the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade cupping for the fasting one and continuous fasting, and did not prohibit them upon his companions. They said: O Messenger of Allah, you fast continuously till the sahar. He said: Though I fast continuously till the sahar, my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, feeds me and gives me drink."
"22296","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Masud ibn al-Hakam al-Ansari, from a man from the companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered Abd Allah ibn Hudhafa al-Sahmi to ride his mount in the days of Mina and proclaim among the people: No one shall fast, for these are days of eating and drinking. He said: I saw him upon his mount calling with that."
"22297","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Mamar, he said: al-Zuhri said, and Abd al-Rahman ibn Kab ibn Malik informed me, and his father was one of the three who were forgiven, from a man from the companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood that day as an orator, and praised Allah and extolled Him, and sought forgiveness for the martyrs who were killed on the Day of Uhud, then said: You, company of Muhajirun, increase, while the Ansar do not increase, and the Ansar are my chest to which I sheltered. Honor their noble and overlook their offender, for they have fulfilled what was upon them, and what is for them remains."
"22689","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Aban narrated to us, Abu Imran narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, and he was a governor over Tawwaj, and he praised him well, from some companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Whoever sleeps upon a rooftop with nothing to keep his feet from falling and falls, protection is freed from him; and whoever rides the sea when it rages is freed from protection."
"22692","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, Husayn narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from a man of his people, who said: I entered upon the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while upon me was a ring of gold, so he took a palm stalk and struck my hand with it, and said: Throw it away. He said: So I went out and threw it away, then returned to him. Then he said: What did the ring do? He said: I said: I threw it away. He said: I only commanded you to benefit from it and not throw it away."
"22694","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abu al-Malih narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Khalid, from his father, from his grandfather, and his grandfather had companionship, that he went out visiting a man of his brothers, then his complaint reached him. He said: So he entered upon him and said: I came to you visiting, visiting the sick, and giving glad tidings. He said: How did you gather all this? He said: I went out intending to visit you, then your complaint reached me, so it was a sick-visit, and I give you glad tidings with something I heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: When a station from Allah has preceded for a servant which he does not reach by his deed, Allah tries him in his body, or in his wealth, or in his child, then makes him patient until He brings him to the station that preceded for him from Him."
"23588","Rawh and Abd al-Razzaq both said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us; Hasan ibn Muslim informed me, from Tawus, from a man who met the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Circumambulation is prayer, so when you circumambulate, lessen speech. And Ibn Bakr did not raise it."
"23589","Yunus narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from al-Ashath ibn Sulaym, from his father, from a man from Banu Yarbu, he said: I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and I heard him speaking to the people, saying: The hand of the giver is upper: your mother, and your father, and your sister, and your brother, then the nearest, the nearest. Then a man said: O Messenger of Allah, these are Banu Thalabah ibn Yarbu who struck so-and-so. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No soul wrongs on behalf of another."
"23590","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from al-Azraq ibn Qays, from Yahya ibn Yamur, from a man from among the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The first of what the servant is judged for is his prayer; if he completed it, it is written for him complete, and if he did not complete it, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: Look, do you find for My servant any voluntary prayer, that you complete thereby his obligation? Then zakat likewise, then deeds are taken according to that."
"23591","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Muhallab ibn Abi Sufrah, from a man from among the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: I do not see them tonight but that they will attack you by night; if they do, your sign is Ha Mim; they will not be aided."
"23592","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Tamimah, from a man from his people, that he came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, or he said: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and a man came to him and said: Are you the Messenger of Allah, or he said: Are you Muhammad? He said: Yes. He said: To what do you call? He said: I call to Allah alone: who, when harm befalls you and you call Him, removes it from you, and who, when a year of drought strikes you and you call Him, grows for you, and who, when you are in a barren land and lose your way and call Him, returns you. He said: Then the man embraced Islam, then said: Advise me, O Messenger of Allah. Then he said to him: Do not revile anything, or he said: anyone, al-Hakam doubted. He said: Then I have not reviled anything, neither a camel nor a sheep, since the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, advised me. And do not disdain kindness, even spreading your face to your brother while you speak to him, and pour from your bucket into the vessel of one seeking water, and wear your lower garment to half the shin; if you refuse, then to the ankles; and beware of dragging the lower garment, for it is from arrogance, and Allah does not love arrogance."
"23593","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Muhajir al-Saigh, from an unnamed man from among the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he heard a man, meaning the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, reciting: Say: O disbelievers, and he said: As for this one, he has been absolved from polytheism; and he heard another reciting: Say: He is Allah, One, and he said: As for this one, he has been forgiven."
"23594","Hasan narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from some of the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cauterized Sad, or Asad ibn Zurarah, in his throat for the inflammation, and said: I leave in myself no distress regarding Sad, or Asad ibn Zurarah."
"23595","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Jafar, from al-Fadl ibn Amr ibn Umayyah, from his father, he said: I heard men narrating from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: When the slave girl is freed, she has the choice as long as he has not had intercourse with her; if she wishes, she leaves him, and if he has intercourse with her, she has no choice and cannot leave him."
"23596","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Abi Jafar narrated to us, from al-Fadl ibn al-Hasan ibn Amr ibn Umayyah al-Damri, he said: I heard men from among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, narrating that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When the slave girl is freed while she is under a slave, her affair is in her hand; if she remains until he has intercourse with her, she is his wife and cannot leave him."
"23859","I heard it alone, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us from Asim ibn Kulayb from his father from a man of the Ansar who said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the funeral of a man of the Ansar, and I was a boy with my father, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat at the edge of the grave pit and kept instructing the digger, saying: Widen from the side of the head, and widen from the side of the feet, for many a cluster of his in Paradise."
"23860","Abdussalam ibn Harb narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abdurrahman al-Dalani narrated to me from Abu al-Ala al-Awdi from Humayd ibn Abdurrahman from a man of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When two callers gather, answer the nearer of them in door, for the nearer of them in door is the nearer of them in neighborhood, and if one of them precedes, answer the one who preceded."
"23861","Abdurrahman ibn Mahdi and Abdurrazzaq narrated to us from Malik from Sumayy from Abu Bakr ibn Abdurrahman from some of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was seen at al-Arj pouring water over his head while fasting, from heat or thirst."
"23862","Sufyan narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Humayd ibn Abdurrahman ibn Awf from a man of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that a man said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Tell me words I may live by, and do not make many upon me lest I forget, he said: Avoid anger, then he repeated to him, so he said: Avoid anger."
"23877","Abdullah ibn al-Walid al-Adani narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Khalid al-Hadhdha narrated to us from Abu Qilabah from Muhammad ibn Abi A'ishah from a man of the companions of Muhammad who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perhaps you recite while the imam recites, he said it three times, they said: We do that, he said: So do not do it, except that one of you recite the Fatihah of the Book."
"23878","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us from Ata from Abu Abdurrahman who said: Those who taught us recitation among the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to us that they would learn ten verses from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and would not take the next ten until they knew what in these of knowledge and action, they said: So we learned knowledge and action."
"23880","Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Khalid al-Hadhdha narrated to us from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar from Ibn Abbas who said: I used to say about the children of the polytheists: They are of them, so a man narrated to me from a man of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I met him and he narrated to me from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Their Lord knows best of them, He created them and He knows best of them and of what they would do."
"23882","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: We heard it from al-A'mash, Abdullah ibn Yasar narrated to me from Abdurrahman ibn Abi Layla from a man of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Were it not that I burden my ummah, I would order them to use the siwak with every prayer."
"23883","Isma'il narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us from Abu Qilabah from a man of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: After you, or behind you, is the lying misleader, and his head from behind is knotted, knotted, and he will say: I am your lord, so whoever says: You lie, you are not our Lord, but Allah is our Lord, and upon Him we rely, and to Him we turn, and we seek refuge in Allah from you, he said: Then he has no way against him."
"23886","Isma'il narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us from Yazid ibn Abi Habib who said: Marthad ibn Abdillah would not come to the mosque but with something to give in charity, he said: So he came one day to the mosque with onions with him, so I said to him: Abu al-Khayr, what do you want with this, it will make your garment stink upon you, he said: O son of my brother, by Allah there was nothing in my house to give in charity but it, a man of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to me from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The shade of the believer on the Day of Resurrection is his charity."
"23887","Isma'il narrated to us, Ata ibn al-Sa'ib informed us from Arfajah from a man of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he mentioned Ramadan and said: In it the gates of Paradise are opened, and in it the gates of Fire are closed, and in it the devils are chained, and in it a caller calls every night: O seeker of good, come, and O seeker of evil, desist, until Ramadan ends."
"23888","Isma'il narrated to us from al-Jurayri from Abu Sakhr al-Uqayli, a man of the Bedouins narrated to me who said: I brought goods to Madinah in the life of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when I finished my sale I said: I shall meet this man and hear from him, he said: He met me between Abu Bakr and Umar walking, so I followed behind them until they came upon a Jew spreading the Torah, reading it, consoling himself with it for a son of his dying, like the finest and most handsome of youths, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I adjure you by the One who sent down the Torah, do you find in your book my description and my advent, so he shook his head thus, meaning no, so his son said: By the One who sent down the Torah, we find in our book your description and your advent, and I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that you are the Messenger of Allah, so he said: Remove the Jews from your brother, then he took charge of his shrouding and embalming and prayed over him."
"23889","Isma'il narrated to us, Khalid al-Hadhdha narrated to us from al-Qasim ibn Rabi'ah from Uqbah ibn Aws, and Isma'il once said: Ya'qub ibn Aws, from a man of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave a sermon at the conquest, and once said: on the day of the conquest of Makkah, and said: There is no god but Allah alone, He kept His promise and helped His servant and routed the confederates alone, indeed every inherited honor claimed and demanded, and blood and wealth, is under these two feet of mine, except the custodianship of the House or the watering of the pilgrims, indeed the victim of mistaken intent, Khalid said, or he said: the victim of mistake resembling intent, the victim of whip and stick, is a hundred camels, among them forty with their young in their bellies."
"23890","Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan narrated to us from Mujalid from Amir from al-Muharrir ibn Abi Hurayrah from a man of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever is afflicted with something in his body and leaves it for Allah, it shall be expiation for him."
"23891","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us from Hisham, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us from Abu Ibrahim al-Ashhali from his father that he came to him and narrated to him, or informed him, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying in the prayer over the dead: O Allah, forgive our living and our dead, our present and our absent, our male and our female, our young and our old."
"23892","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Abu Ghifar narrated to us, Alqamah ibn Abdillah al-Muzani narrated to me, a man of my people narrated to me that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his guest, three times, whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him do good to his neighbor, whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him say good or be silent."
"23893","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, Amr ibn Murrah narrated to me who said: I heard Murrah who said: A man of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to me who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us upon a red mu khadramah she-camel and said: Do you know what day of yours this is, he said: We said: The day of sacrifice, he said: You spoke true, the day of the greater Hajj, do you know what month of yours this is, we said: Dhulhijjah, he said: You spoke true, the deaf month of Allah, do you know what land of yours this is, he said: We said: Al-Mash'ar al-Haram, he said: You spoke true, he said: Your blood and your wealth are sacred to you like the sanctity of this day of yours, in this month of yours, in this land of yours, or he said: like the sanctity of this day of yours and this month of yours and this land of yours, indeed I precede you at the Hawd awaiting you, and I shall outnumber nations through you, so do not blacken my face, indeed you have seen me and heard from me, and you shall be asked about me, so whoever lies upon me, let him take his seat in the Fire, indeed I shall rescue men or women, and others shall be rescued from me, so I shall say: O Lord, my companions, so it shall be said: You do not know what they innovated after you."
"24049","Narrated to us Abd al-Rahman and Abd al-Razzaq, from Malik, from Sumayy, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman, from some of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was seen at al-Arj pouring water on his head from heat or thirst, while he was fasting."
